{%- comment -%}
  GPU numerical computing: sparse LU factorisation of an 8 x 8 circuit-like matrix (structurally symmetric, nonzeros
  as solid dots, zeros as faint points). Eliminating column k with the pivot (accent ring) creates fill-in: new nonzeros
  (rings) at (3,6), (6,3) from pivot 1 and (5,6), (6,5) from pivot 3. At rest the factorisation is done and the
  triangles L (below the diagonal) and U (the diagonal and above) stand apart.
  Live: L and U close up, the fill-in clears, the pivot runs down the diagonal with the elimination front (the trailing
  submatrix) shrinking behind it, the fill-in appears where it is created, and L and U part again (diagrams.js, SCENES.hpc).
  Parameters: live (hover | always | off), trigger (view | manual), detail ("full" shows the labels), class.
{%- endcomment -%}
<svg class="diagram diagram--hpc{% if include.class %} {{ include.class }}{% endif %}" viewBox="0 0 320 180" data-kit="diagram" data-live="{{ include.live | default: 'hover' }}" data-trigger="{{ include.trigger | default: 'view' }}"{% if include.detail == 'full' %} data-detail="full"{% endif %} role="img" aria-label="A sparse matrix factorised into lower and upper triangles: a pivot runs down the diagonal, a few new nonzeros of fill-in appear, and the two triangles separate." fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
  {%- comment -%} the elimination front (live only): the trailing submatrix, shrinking towards the corner {%- endcomment %}
  <rect class="dg-h dg-x" data-dg="front" x="96" y="26" width="128" height="128" opacity="0"/>
  {%- comment -%} L: the lower triangle {%- endcomment %}
